mindmap
  root(("HTTP & Web Technologies"))
    HTTP Protocol Evolution
      HTTP/0.9 (1991)
        Single-line request
        HTML response only
      HTTP/1.0 (1996)
        Request/response headers
        Status codes
        New connection per request
      HTTP/1.1 (1999)
        Persistent connections (keep-alive)
        Pipelining
        Host header (virtual hosting)
        Chunked transfer encoding
        Cache-Control, ETag
      HTTP/2 (2015)
        Binary framing layer
        Multiplexed streams
        Server push
        HPACK header compression
        Stream prioritization
      HTTP/3 (2022)
        QUIC transport (UDP-based)
        No TCP head-of-line blocking
        0-RTT connection establishment
        QPACK header compression
        Connection migration
    Request-Response Model
      HTTP Methods
        GET (idempotent, safe)
        POST (create resource)
        PUT (replace resource)
        PATCH (partial update)
        DELETE (remove resource)
        HEAD, OPTIONS, CONNECT, TRACE
      Status Code Classes
        1xx Informational (Continue, Switching)
        2xx Success (OK, Created, No Content)
        3xx Redirection (Moved, Found, Not Modified)
        4xx Client Error (Bad Request, Not Found, Forbidden)
        5xx Server Error (Internal, Gateway Timeout)
      Headers
        General (Date, Connection, Cache-Control)
        Request (Host, User-Agent, Accept, Cookie)
        Response (Content-Type, Set-Cookie, Location)
        Entity (Content-Length, Content-Encoding, ETag)
    Web Infrastructure
      TLS/SSL
        Certificate validation
        Handshake (1-RTT / 0-RTT)
        HTTPS (port 443)
      Content Delivery Networks
        Edge caching (PoPs)
        Cache hit / miss
        CDN providers (CloudFront, Cloudflare, Akamai)
      WebSockets
        Full-duplex over TCP
        Upgrade handshake
        Real-time applications (chat, gaming)
      API Technologies
        REST (resources, methods, HATEOAS)
        GraphQL (client-driven queries, single endpoint)
        gRPC (Protocol Buffers, HTTP/2, streaming)
        SSE (server push, text/event-stream)
    Web Performance
      Caching Strategies
        Browser cache (private)
        CDN cache (shared)
        Cache-Control directives (max-age, s-maxage)
        ETag / Last-Modified validation
      Optimization Techniques
        Minification (HTML, CSS, JS)
        Image optimization (WebP, AVIF)
        Lazy loading
        Preconnect / Preload / Prefetch
        Critical CSS inlining